 wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-write-008", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Over Burrow Roman Fort likely rose on a slight prominence northwest of where Leck Beck meets the River Lune, to command a crossing; its clay-and-turf ramparts hint at a second occupation."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-check-008 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the fort was likely built on a slight prominence [S2]; the prominence is northwest of the confluence of Leck Beck and the River Lune [S2]; the fort was likely built to command a crossing [S2]; the ramparts are of clay and turf [S5]; the excavated ramparts suggest a second occupation [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-verify-024 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Over Burrow Roman Fort is a former Roman fort at Over Burrow (Burrow-in-Lonsdale), Lancashire, North West England [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Over_Burrow_Roman_Fort]; The fort was likely built on a slight prominence northwest of the confluence of Leck Beck with the River Lune [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Over_Burrow_Roman_Fort]; The fort''s position was to command a crossing over the river [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Over_Burrow_Roman_Fort]; The fort had clay-and-turf ramparts, which were archaeologically excavated [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Over_Burrow_Roman_Fort]; The clay-and-turf ramparts suggest a second period of occupation (hint, not proof) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Over_Burrow_Roman_Fort]"}]'::jsonb),
