 {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-check-013 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Homer''s Catalogue of Ships says Lindus took part in the war against Troy [S2]; Lindus has a sanctuary of Athena [S4]; the sanctuary of Athena is revered [S4]; the sanctuary was believed to have been built by Danaus, or according to others by his daughters [S5]; the daughters built it on their flight from Egypt [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-verify-038 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Lindus (Lindos) is an ancient city and archaeological site on the island of Rhodes, Greece [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lindos]; The Catalogue of Ships is the passage in Book 2 of Homer''s Iliad listing the contingents that sailed to Troy [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catalogue_of_Ships]; In the Iliad Book 2 catalogue the Rhodian contingent under Tlepolemus, sent to Troy, dwelt in Lindos, Ialysus and Cameirus, so Lindus took part in the war against Troy [SUPPORTED: https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Perseus:text:1999.01.0134:book=2:card=653]; Lindos had a sanctuary of Athena (the Temple of Athena Lindia) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Athena_Lindia]; The sanctuary of Athena at Lindos was revered (a significant Pan-Hellenic shrine) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Athena_Lindia]; The sanctuary was believed to have been founded by Danaus [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Athena_Lindia]; The sanctuary was said to have been founded by the daughters of Danaus when they landed there in their flight from the sons of Aegyptus [SUPPORTED: https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Perseus:text:1999.01.0126:book=2:chapter=182]"}]'::jsonb),
