e": "Nuragic complex of sa Sedda \''e sos Carros", "changes": "sentences selected and shortened", "licence_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}, "desc_sha256": "2512c223a8f7e41663958bad35cd3681bd1f55089ecb1e2c97fa675dd0c15f15"}}'' restored on Nuragic Complex of Sa Sedda e Sos Carros', '2512c223a8f7e41663958bad35cd3681bd1f55089ecb1e2c97fa675dd0c15f15', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-write-013", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Water once poured from the mouths of ram-shaped protomes into a central basin at the Nuragic Complex of Sa Sedda e Sos Carros, a fountain and a foundry where iron slags were found."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-check-013 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "water once poured from the mouths of ram-shaped protomes [S5]; the water flowed into a central basin [S5]; this was at the Nuragic Complex of Sa Sedda e Sos Carros [S1, S5]; the structure was a fountain [S4]; the site was also a foundry [S6]; iron slags were found there [S6]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-verify-038 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Nuragic complex of sa Sedda ''e sos Carros is an archaeological site (Nuragic, late Bronze Age and early Iron Age) in the territory of Oliena, Sardinia [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuragic_complex_of_sa_Sedda_%27e_sos_Carros]; The complex includes a fountain (a roundhouse with basin) that worked through a hydraulic system [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuragic_complex_of_sa_Sedda_%27e_sos_Carros]; Water arrived through the mouths of ram-shaped protomes into the central basin [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuragic_complex_of_sa_Sedda_%27e_sos_Carros]; Ram (mouflon) heads carved on the walls of the circular room let water flow into the central basin (second source) [SUPPORTED: https://www.sardegnacultura.it/en/articles/oliena-villaggio-nuragico-sa-sedda-e-sos-carros]; The site was a metallurgical centre with a foundry [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuragic_complex_of_sa_Sedda_%27e_sos_Carros]; Iron slags were recovered during the archaeological excavations [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuragic_complex_of_sa_Sedda_%27e_sos_Carros]"}]'::jsonb),
